		{
			"id": "eSV4YH0v50SFBkOMZ",
			"description": "Fire Warrior Combat Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nRigid composite plates: no blunt-trauma rule. Weak Points 5. Full coverage; the helmet carries the comm-link and display. Not vacuum-rated: a sealed void suit is a separate item.\n\nLore: The Fire Warrior's plate: Codex: T'au Empire background describes shas'la wearing light composite armour with a helmet display and comm-link, protective enough to survive a battlefield of small arms but not built for the melee the T'au avoid. The lore fixes the class, not the numbers.\n\nDesign: Anchor (framework): composite plates, DR 70 (carapace class), Weak Points 5, eye 20. Torso DR and eye lens are held exactly. The limbs follow carapace: arms and legs 58 (12 under the torso, as Astartes plate), neck 52 (as Guard carapace), helmet 64 (as Guard carapace), face 36, and hands and feet 36 and 42 (the Tempestus pattern's gauntlets and boots; the Guard's carapace leaves hands bare). Exact odds against the torso (DR 70, WP 5): lasgun 7d(2) 0.6% (4.9% with WP 5); autogun 7d 0.0%; boltgun or pulse rifle 6dx2(2) 79.4% (80.4% with WP 5); heavy bolter 7dx2(2) 93.9% (94.2% with WP 5); plasma gun 6dx4(3) 100.0%. So it is carapace exactly: lasgun 0.6% (4.9% with the Weak Points chance), a pulse rifle 79.4% (T'au fire on T'au) and a Marine's bolter 79.4%; a shuriken catapult hit (5d(3) cut) gets through 5.9% (10.0% with WP). Arms and legs (DR 58): pulse rifle 93.9%, lasgun 13.7%. Eye lens (DR 20): a lasgun hit penetrates 100.0% of the time, a pulse rifle 100.0%; an eye hit is a brain hit for piercing and tight-beam burning damage (B399), and a random face hit strikes an eye on 1 in 6 (about 0.5% of random hits). Weight 25 lb against the Guard carapace's 30 lb (T'au composite is lighter), cost $3,000 against $1,800, priced above the Guard's carapace for its integrated helmet display and comm-link (design numbers). LC 0: xenos-made.",
