		{
			"id": "eKVwVM6Gfji00BWYF",
			"description": "Recon Armour, Pathfinder Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 5: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 5 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47): a hit that fails to penetrate still delivers (damage/10, rounded down, minimum 1) crushing injury. The helmet carries a sensor suite and comm-link (background). No DX or Stealth penalty.\n\nLore: The light armour of the T'au scout: Codex: T'au Empire background shows Pathfinders in lighter armour than a Fire Warrior, since they scout ahead of the line and rely on cover, camouflage and their markerlights rather than plate.\n\nDesign: Anchor (framework): flexible, DR 36, Weak Points 5, the mesh anchor. Torso DR and Weak Points are held exactly, the same protection as Guardian and Kabalite mesh. Exact odds against the torso (DR 36, WP 5): lasgun 7d(2) 90.6% (91.0% with WP 5); autogun 7d 0.3% (4.5% with WP 5); boltgun or pulse rifle 6dx2(2) 99.8%; heavy bolter 7dx2(2) 100.0%; plasma gun 6dx4(3) 100.0%. So a lasgun goes through 90.6% of the time and a pulse rifle always; only slug-throwers such as the autogun (0.3%), light blades and shrapnel are stopped. Limbs 29, neck 21, as mesh; helmet 30, face 25 and eye 15 for a light helm with a sensor visor, hands and feet 18. Eye lens (DR 15): lasgun 100.0%. Weight 12 lb (mesh is 6 lb; recon armour also carries the helmet and boots), cost $2,200 (mesh $1,600; the sensor helmet is the difference).",
