		{
			"id": "eRvGW2QIR2OcBS9cT",
			"description": "Kroot Hide and Scavenged Plate",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 8: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 8 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nFlexible armour (B47): blunt-trauma rules apply. Covers torso, arms and legs only; head, hands and feet are bare. Crude and patched: Weak Points 8. Kroot are not slowed by it: no DX or Move penalty.\n\nLore: Kroot fight in hide and whatever they have picked off the dead: background shows them in light, cobbled-together protection, sometimes scavenged plates and scraps of enemy armour, never in formal issue. This entry stands for the typical kit; no source gives its exact contents.\n\nDesign: The framework fixes only 'light' for Kroot armour, so it sits well under flak (30): torso DR 15, arms and legs 8, and no protection elsewhere. Weak Points 8 (like Ork scrap plate, which the framework gives 7-8) for its gaps. Exact odds against the torso (DR 15, WP 8): lasgun 100.0%, autogun 97.8%, pulse rifle 100.0%: it stops light blades, pistol rounds and shrapnel and little else. Weight 12 lb, cost $150, TL 4 (hide and hammered scrap: the gear itself is low-tech even when the plate was scavenged from a high-tech source).",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Xenos",
				"T'au",
				"Kroot"
			],
			"tech_level": "4",
