		{
			"id": "EqziOeZ5YuScCepNl",
			"description": "XV25 Stealth Battlesuit",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 4: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 4 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nBattlesuit rules. Sealed pilot: the suit is airtight against hostile atmospheres; extended vacuum operation is the GM's call. It needs trained handling: an untrained wearer is at -4 to all DX rolls and cannot use linked fire or the support systems. Linked fire (house rule, since GURPS lets one Attack maneuver fire one weapon): the pilot may fire all mounted weapons in one Attack maneuver at one target, rolling separately for each at -1 per weapon beyond the first that turn. A Multi-tracker removes that penalty and a Target Lock lets weapons fire at different targets (see those items). Size: about 2 m, SM 0 (framework gives no size; a stealth suit is slighter than a Crisis). One weapon hardpoint and one support hardpoint. GCS adds a container's children to its own weight and cost: the shell alone is 95 lb and $40,000; with its five children (119 lb, $77,000) the assembled suit is 214 lb and $117,000. The servo bonus lives on the Servo-Motor child only, so it is counted once. The stealth field and jump jets are separate children, so they can be damaged or removed separately.\n\nLore: The T'au scout-suit: Codex: T'au Empire background describes the XV25 Stealth battlesuit as a light infiltration suit that hides its wearer with a stealth field and jumps in on jump jets, carrying a burst cannon or fusion blaster, for hit-and-run strikes behind the enemy line. The framework fixes its DR and features; sizes and weights are design numbers.\n\nDesign: Anchor (framework): DR 85, Weak Points 4, stealth field (a large visual-concealment bonus, not DR), jump jets. Torso DR 85, WP 4 held exactly; limbs 73 (12 under the torso, as Astartes plate), neck 55, helmet 85, face 63 (25 under), hands 50 and feet 63; eye lens 35 (scaled from the Crisis's anchored 45 at DR 110, about 41% of torso: 41% x 85). Exact odds against the torso (DR 85, WP 4): lasgun 7d(2) 0.0% (1.4% with WP 4); autogun 7d 0.0%; boltgun or pulse rifle 6dx2(2) 45.4% (46.4% with WP 4); heavy bolter 7dx2(2) 74.3% (74.8% with WP 4); plasma gun 6dx4(3) 100.0%; autocannon 6dx3(3) 99.8%; krak missile 6dx6(3) 100.0%; lascannon 8dx8(5) 100.0%; meltagun, short range 8dx6(10) 100.0%; Astartes power sword at ST 30, 8d+3(10) 100.0%. So it is Sororitas-grade plate (DR 85): a lasgun is stopped (1.4% with the Weak Points chance), a pulse rifle or a bolter goes through 45.4% of the time (the framework's Sororitas figure) and a heavy bolter 74%, and it does not stop plasma or anti-armour weapons. Eye lens (DR 35): lasgun 93.9%, boltgun 99.9%, plasma 100.0% (those are per eye hit; a random face hit is 1 in 6 an eye). Weight: shell 95 lb, 1.1 lb per DR point (Mk VII's shell is 1.5 lb per point; the Stealth suit's plates are thinner and it relies on the field), children 119 lb. Servo bonus Lifting +10 and Striking +5: enough to bring the pilot (ST 11) to 21 for the 45 lb burst cannon (Min ST 21M) and no more. Cost $40,000 for the shell, level with a Mk VII's plate; the stealth field is the expensive part, $45,000 as its own child.",
