			"children": [
				{
					"id": "ef-sok3q2EBtBwmtr",
					"description": "Servo-Motor Actuators (Stealth Pattern)",
					"local_notes": "Powered strength for the suit: Lifting ST +10 and Striking ST +5. Counted only here; the parent has no ST bonus.\n\nLore: The suit's servos let its pilot carry a heavy weapon and jump with it; no source gives figures.\n\nDesign: Sized to just meet the burst cannon's Min ST 21M (11 + 10). A lighter package than the Crisis's (+18/+9) since a stealth suit is smaller and lighter.",
					"tech_level": "11",
					"legality_class": "0",
					"base_value": "16000",
					"base_weight": "60 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "lifting_st",
							"amount": 10
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "striking_st",
							"amount": 5
						}
					],
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "e6YbFbb7SobtY4Stj",
					"description": "Stealth Field Generator",
					"local_notes": "Scatters and bends light around the wearer: +6 to Stealth, and Vision rolls to spot the suit are at -6. Once the wearer is spotted, ranged attackers beyond 10 yards who rely on sight alone are at -3 to hit. It is a visual effect only: thermal, motion, audio and non-visual sensors see the suit normally, and it fails within 2 yards. Firing does not break it. No DR.\n\nLore: The stealth field is the XV25's defining feature in background, a large visual-concealment bonus, not armour; the exact ranges are not fixed in the sources.\n\nDesign: Framework: 'a large visual-concealment bonus, not DR'. +6 Stealth (a large bonus: an Invisibility-lite of the Aeldari kind), -6 to spot, a further -3 to be hit at range when the wearer is spotted but only seen by sight; the 10-yard threshold and 2-yard failure are design choices to keep it from being an invisibility cloak.",
					"tech_level": "11",
					"legality_class": "0",
					"base_value": "45000",
					"base_weight": "12 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Stealth"
							},
							"amount": 6
						}
					],
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eneFg4abD6kxkSndu",
					"description": "Jump Jets (Stealth Pattern)",
					"local_notes": "Flight, in short hops: Air Move 10, 4 seconds of thrust per fuel load (each turn of thrust uses 1), no hover: the pilot climbs on burn turns and must be descending or landing when the fuel is gone. A burning jump carries the suit about 30 yards up and 50 across. Refuel about 10 minutes. Exhaust wash 1d burn to anyone within 2 yards of a landing.\n\nLore: Jump jets, per framework: the stealth suit hops in and out of cover on them rather than flying.\n\nDesign: Scaled from the Astartes jump pack (Air Move 15, 6 s, 60 lb) and Sororitas pack (Air Move 10, 4 s, 30 lb) since a Stealth suit is lighter than either wearer.",
					"tech_level": "11",
					"legality_class": "0",
					"base_value": "5000",
					"base_weight": "25 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eFdkoAKGo0KKxQAFG",
					"description": "Cockpit Interface, Sensors and Life Support (Stealth Pattern)",
					"local_notes": "Sealed cockpit, comm-link, display and sensor suite. +1 to Observation.\n\nLore: Battlesuit pilots fight by instruments; the suit's interface is the reason a T'au can fight in it.\n\nDesign: Flat +1, less than an Astartes auto-senses suite's +2 since it is a basic package. Flavour subsystem.",
					"tech_level": "11",
					"legality_class": "0",
					"base_value": "8000",
					"base_weight": "12 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Observation"
							},
							"amount": 1
						}
					],
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "ef2SYJBY0MthaKPCW",
					"description": "Hardpoint Mounts (Stealth Pattern)",
					"local_notes": "One weapon hardpoint (burst cannon or fusion blaster) and one support-system hardpoint. The weapons and systems are separate items and are not included.\n\nLore: Battlesuits are modular: the weapon and support items fitted are the pilot's choice.\n\nDesign: The mounting hardware, priced apart from what it carries.",
					"tech_level": "11",
					"legality_class": "0",
					"base_value": "3000",
					"base_weight": "10 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "ET21pE784NBoJDHdt",
			"description": "XV8 Crisis Battlesuit",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 3: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 3 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nBattlesuit rules. Sealed pilot: the suit is airtight against hostile atmospheres; extended vacuum operation is the GM's call. It needs trained handling: an untrained wearer is at -4 to all DX rolls and cannot use linked fire or the support systems. Linked fire (house rule, since GURPS lets one Attack maneuver fire one weapon): the pilot may fire all mounted weapons in one Attack maneuver at one target, rolling separately for each at -1 per weapon beyond the first that turn. A Multi-tracker removes that penalty and a Target Lock lets weapons fire at different targets (see those items). Size: about 2.5 m, SM +1 while worn (a bigger target, +1 to be hit; also the larger reach of its stride). Three hardpoints, each carrying one weapon or one support system (see the Hardpoint Mounts child); no weapons are pre-loaded. GCS adds a container's children to its own weight and cost: the shell alone is 165 lb and $45,000; with its five children (261 lb, $71,000) the assembled suit is 426 lb and $116,000. Servo ST lives on the Servo-Motor child only, so it is counted once.\n\nLore: The T'au's signature battlesuit: Codex: T'au Empire background shows the XV8 Crisis as a jet-pack-equipped assault suit, armed by choice from a list of burst cannons, plasma, fusion, missile and flamer weapons on three hardpoints and piloted by a Shas'ui or Shas'vre, and as the suit in which the T'au best show their doctrine of fast, heavily-armed hit-and-shoot mobile warfare. The framework fixes DR, Weak Points, eye lens, size, servo ST, jet pack and hardpoints; weights and costs are design numbers.\n\nDesign: Anchor (framework): DR 110, Weak Points 3, eye 45, about 2.5 m (SM +1), servo ST as a child, jet pack, three hardpoints. Torso 110, WP 3 and eye 45 held exactly. Limbs 98 (12 under, as Astartes plate), neck 75, helmet 110, face 85 (25 under), hands 68, feet 85. Exact odds against the torso (DR 110, WP 3): lasgun 7d(2) 0.0% (0.1% with WP 3); autogun 7d 0.0%; boltgun or pulse rifle 6dx2(2) 6.1% (6.5% with WP 3); heavy bolter 7dx2(2) 25.7% (26.1% with WP 3); plasma gun 6dx4(3) 99.8%; autocannon 6dx3(3) 98.0%; krak missile 6dx6(3) 100.0%; lascannon 8dx8(5) 100.0%; meltagun, short range 8dx6(10) 100.0%; Astartes power sword at ST 30, 8d+3(10) 100.0%. So it is a shade over Astartes plate: a lasgun almost never hurts it (0.1% with the Weak Points chance), a pulse rifle or bolter gets through 6.1% of the time (Astartes plate 14.5%), a heavy bolter 25.7%; anti-armour weapons (autocannon 98%, plasma 99.8%, meltagun, lascannon, krak 100%) go through, so massed pulse and bolter fire is a real threat and heavy weapons kill it. Eye lens (DR 45): lasgun 66.8%, boltgun 99.0%, plasma 100.0%: a lasgun hit strikes a Crisis eye lens through 66.8% of the time, a brain hit for piercing/burn damage (B399), the suit's honest weak spot; a random face hit strikes an eye on 1 in 6. Weight: shell 165 lb, 1.5 lb per DR point (the Astartes and Terminator shells are 1.5 lb per point), children 261 lb. Servo Lifting +18 / Striking +9: with a pilot ST 11 the suit lifts as ST 29 and swings as ST 20, enough for a missile pod (21M), a plasma rifle (17M) or a cyclic ion blaster (21M) with room to spare. Cost: shell $45,000, servos $38,000, jets $18,000, hardpoints $6,000, cockpit $9,000: $116,000 assembled.",
