				{
					"id": "echx6kAoRzLQMxn6j",
					"description": "Servo-Motor Actuators (Crisis Pattern)",
					"local_notes": "Powered strength for the suit: Lifting ST +18 and Striking ST +9. Counted only here; the parent has no ST bonus. Min ST of mounted weapons is checked against pilot ST + Lifting ST.\n\nLore: Battlesuit servos let a T'au of ordinary strength carry weapons that a Marine would find heavy.\n\nDesign: Sized for the heaviest common Crisis weapon (46 lb missile pod, Min ST 21M: 11+18 = 29) with a margin. Well above the Astartes Mk VII's +9/+5 because a T'au pilot starts at ST 11 rather than ST 30: the suit has to supply most of the strength (29 lifting against a Marine in Mk VII's 39).",
					"tech_level": "11",
					"legality_class": "0",
					"base_value": "38000",
					"base_weight": "150 lb",
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "lifting_st",
							"amount": 18
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "striking_st",
							"amount": 9
